  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 8.4(a), the weighted supermatrix W for the ANP example — a screenshot titled \"Super Decisions Main Window: Chapter_8_ANP.sdmod\". Clusters are L1-GOAL (Goal_Node), L2-Criteria (C1-C3) and L3-Alternatives (A1, A2). Unlike the AHP matrix in Figure 8.2(b), the criteria-to-criteria block is not zero (C1 column: C2 0.083333, C3 0.166667; C2 column: C1 0.125000, C3 0.125000; C3 column: C1 0.187500, C2 0.062500) and the alternatives feed back into the criteria (A1 column: C2 0.333333, C3 0.666667; A2 column: C2 0.500000, C3 0.500000). That non-zero feedback is the structural difference the chapter is illustrating.",
